      en: ["The complex is surrounded by a 74 x 74 meter stone wall.", "Candi Mahligai, the tallest structure, stands approximately 14 meters high.", "Unlike Javanese temples made of andesite, these are built of red clay bricks.", "Located near the Kampar Kanan River, a vital ancient trade artery.", "Likely served as a religious center for the maritime Srivijaya Empire.", "The stupa's shape is unique in Indonesia, showing some Thai or Indian influence.", "First described by European explorers in the mid-19th century.", "A major site for the celebration of Vesak by Sumatran Buddhists today."]
