      en: ["The name 'Lawang Sewu' is a local nickname; it has about 600-700 doors.", "Designed by Dutch architects Cosman Citroen and B.J. Ouëndag.", "Features magnificent stained-glass windows from the city of Delft, Netherlands.", "Served as the headquarters of the national railway company (PT KAI).", "The site of the 'Five-Day Battle in Semarang' against the Japanese in 1945.", "Restored by PT KAI in 2009 to its original colonial-era glory.", "Known for its underground tunnel system used for cooling and storage.", "Consistently ranked as one of Indonesia's most haunted locations by ghost hunters."]
