      en: ["Founded by Sultan Hamengkubuwono I in 1755 after the Giyanti Treaty.", "The palace is aligned on a straight line between Mount Merapi and the South Sea.", "Home to the 'Kyai Guntur Madu' and 'Kyai Nagawilaga' sacred Gamelan sets.", "The main audience hall, Bangsal Kencana, features gold-leafed teak pillars.", "The 'Abdi Dalem' servants wear traditional Javanese dress as their uniform.", "Contains a museum dedicated to the 9th Sultan, a national hero of Indonesia.", "The Kraton acts as the official office of the Governor of Yogyakarta.", "Hosts daily performances of Javanese wayang, dance, and music for the public."]
