      en: ["Inaugurated on October 12, 2004, exactly two years after the attack.", "Lists the names of 202 victims from 22 different nations.", "The largest number of victims were from Australia (88) and Indonesia (38).", "Located on Jalan Legian, where the Paddy's Pub and Sari Club once stood.", "The intricate stone carving represents the 'Kayon' (Tree of Life).", "A site of international pilgrimage for families of the victims.", "Symbolizes Bali's recovery and its 'Tri Hita Karana' philosophy of harmony.", "Surrounded by the bustling tourist district of Kuta."]
