      en: "The National Monument, or Monas, is the defining landmark of Jakarta and the supreme symbol of Indonesia's struggle for independence. Standing 132 meters tall in the center of Merdeka Square, the monument is topped by a 14.5-meter 'Flame of Independence' coated with 50 kilograms of gold leaf. Its design incorporates the Hindu-Buddhist symbols of Lingam (stability) and Yoni (fertility), reflecting the nation's deep historical roots. The base of the monument houses the National History Museum, which features 51 dioramas depicting Indonesia's journey from prehistory through the colonial era to the proclamation of independence in 1945. Monas is a site of immense national pride and the focal point for major national celebrations and public gatherings. Geography K9 — National Symbols and Post-Colonial Identity."
